      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? specifically for a shipment of electronics",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller of the electronics is responsible for delivering goods to the named port of destination, including procuring marine insurance and bearing all risks associated with transport up to that point. They must also pay all packaging, freight, and export-related costs, though they do not bear the risk of loss once the goods are loaded on the vessel. However, this responsibility ends regarding the transport itself; any costs such as port charges or taxes at the destination port lie with the buyer, even if the seller booked the original freight.",
