    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. but just to be clear, if the ship encounters a storm or something and the cargo gets damaged before it hits the destination port, who is actually the one dealing with the insurance claim process? is it still the seller or does it fall on us?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF terms, you (the buyer) are the party named in the insurance policy and are responsible for handling any claims arising from damage or loss during transit, even though the seller secured the insurance and bore the financial cost for it. The seller has only obligated themselves to procure coverage for the minimum amount for a \"total case\" without deducting salvage value and to provide you with the necessary insurance certificate; they do not share in the cost of the claim if the cargo is lost. Consequently, if electronics are damaged due to a storm, you must negotiate with your insurance provider and work with the carrier or subrogated insurer to recover losses.",
